  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Ramos carried the lineup on his back, and that swing in the eighth defined a blowout that never felt close.",
    "what_this_means": "This team doesn't need suspense. Heliot Ramos supplied 5 RBI on two homers, and once the sixth inning arrived with five runs already on the board, Toronto was watching the game from behind glass. The offense converted just four of seventeen RISP situations, but it didn't matter. Those four conversions arrived in high-leverage moments where they compounded fast. A 10-1 margin is not a statement this team makes often. Landen Roupp threw 8 scoreless innings through five, then Ramos did what the bullpen didn't need to do: he made late insurance look like mercy. Spencer Bivens closed it with two strikeouts in one perfect inning, unnecessary and clean. Fragile streaks don't end on nights like this. They end when the lineup finds its leverage and doesn't waste it.",
    "what_to_watch": "Toronto ranks 28th in the majors in runs scored. Trevor McDonald draws a favorable matchup tonight at 6:45 PT. If he commands his fastball and locates the breaking stuff early, the Giants' defense can handle the rest.",
